{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 60, :comments ["<b>And may your seed possess the gate of those who hate him.</b> To Abraham too this same expression was spoken — ״וְיִירַשׁ זַרְעֲךָ אֵת שַׁעַר אֹיְבָיו״, for such is the measure for all who perform kindness, that they have many friends, as it is written (Proverbs 19:6) ״רַבִּים יְחַלּוּ פְנֵי נָדִיב וְכָל הָרֵעַ לְאִישׁ מַתָּן״. And Abraham performed kindness with everyone — with those near and those far — and so too Rebecca. Therefore, by way of nature, they would possess the gate of their enemies, for they have many friends who stand by them in their time of trouble, as our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Bava Kamma 17a) ״כָּל הָעוֹסֵק בַּתּוֹרָה וּבִגְמִילוּת חֲסָדִים זוֹכֶה לְנַחֲלַת שְׁנֵי שְׁבָטִים״ etc. And it concludes there: ״אִכָּא דְּאָמְרֵי אוֹיְבָיו נוֹפְלִים לְפָנָיו חֲלָלִים כְּיוֹסֵף״ — his enemies fall slain before him like Joseph, as it is said (Deuteronomy 33:17) ״בְּכוֹר שׁוֹרוֹ הָדָר לוֹ וְקַרְנֵי רְאֵם קַרְנָיו״ etc. For Joseph too performed kindness with all his father's household and with those far off during both years of famine, and so David said (Psalms 112:5) ״טוֹב אִישׁ חוֹנֵן וּמַלְוֶה״ etc. ״סָמוּךְ לִבּוֹ לֹא יִירָא עַד אֲשֶׁר יִרְאֶה בְצָרָיו, פִּזַּר נָתַן לָאֶבְיוֹנִים, קַרְנוֹ תָּרוּם בְּכָבוֹד״ — for with his horn he shall gore peoples like Joseph. Therefore they said to her ״הֲיִי לְאַלְפֵי רְבָבָה״ — but did they set a limit to her blessing? For what is the distinction? Any person who has children — given the multiplication of days — will produce from himself this number and more than that! Rather, it is certain that they were not speaking of those who issue from her loins, for they were assured by the power of this elder Abraham, who had already been blessed that his seed would be as the sand of the sea. And what is the meaning of what they said, ״לְאַלְפֵי רְבָבָה״? This teaches: what is the force of ״לְאַלְפֵי״? Rather, they said: may it be His will that you merit to do good and to perform kindness for thousands and ten thousands, for your host shall be great, and through this you will have many friends, and by this cause your seed shall possess the gate of his enemies, for many will stand to help you when you go forth to war. And it is also possible that by way of counsel they said this to her, and in this the expression ״הֲיִי לְאַלְפֵי רְבָבָה״ is precisely calibrated. And from the fact that it used the expression ״וְיִירַשׁ״ — hear from this that they said to her: do not worry about the expenditure, but rather ״שַׁלַּח לַחְמְךָ עַל פְּנֵי הַמַּיִם״ to thousands and ten thousands of men, and in the end you will receive an inheritance in the gate of those who hate you doubled twofold, for there is one who scatters yet increases."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The phrase אביוונ (appearing as לאביונים in standard Psalms text) is normalized to לָאֶבְיוֹנִים per the biblical verse cited (Psalms 112:9)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:29:56.196419173Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}